1	# Contract: `ChatBloc` (`lib/features/chat/presentation/bloc/chat_bloc.dart`)
2	
3	```dart
4	class ChatBloc extends Bloc<ChatEvent, ChatState> {
5	  ChatBloc({required ChatRepository chatRepository, required ConnectivityChecker connectivityChecker})
6	      : _chatRepository = chatRepository, // ignore: prefer_initializing_formals
7	        _connectivityChecker = connectivityChecker, // ignore: prefer_initializing_formals
8	        super(const ChatLoading()) {
9	    on<ChatStarted>(_onStarted);
10	    on<ConversationSelected>(_onConversationSelected);
11	    on<NewConversationRequested>(_onNewConversationRequested);
12	    on<MessageSubmitted>(_onMessageSubmitted);
13	    on<MessageRetryRequested>(_onMessageRetryRequested);
14	    on<_ConnectivityChanged>(_onConnectivityChanged);
15	    _connectivitySubscription = connectivityChecker.onConnectivityChanged.listen(
16	      (isOnline) => add(_ConnectivityChanged(isOnline)),
17	    );
18	  }
19	
20	  final ChatRepository _chatRepository;
21	  final ConnectivityChecker _connectivityChecker;
22	  late final StreamSubscription<bool> _connectivitySubscription;
23	  final _reauthController = StreamController<void>.broadcast();
24	  int _turnGeneration = 0;   // guards against a resolved/superseded turn's late emit (defensive; see research.md R9)
25	
26	  Stream<void> get reauthRequired => _reauthController.stream;
27	}
28	```
29	
30	## `ChatStarted` — resume last session or show empty state
31	
32	```dart
33	Future<void> _onStarted(ChatStarted event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
34	  final isOnline = await _connectivityChecker.hasConnection();
35	  final lastId = await _chatRepository.lastActiveSessionId;
36	  if (lastId == null) {
37	    emit(ChatReady(sessionId: null, messages: const [], isOffline: !isOnline, awaitingResponse: false));
38	    return;
39	  }
40	  await _loadSession(lastId, emit, isOffline: !isOnline);
41	}
42	```
43	
44	## `ConversationSelected` / `NewConversationRequested`
45	
46	```dart
47	Future<void> _onConversationSelected(ConversationSelected event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
48	  _turnGeneration++;   // invalidate any in-flight turn from the conversation being left (spec.md Edge Cases)
49	  final isOnline = await _connectivityChecker.hasConnection();
50	  await _loadSession(event.sessionId, emit, isOffline: !isOnline);
51	}
52	
53	Future<void> _onNewConversationRequested(NewConversationRequested event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
54	  _turnGeneration++;   // same rationale as above
55	  final current = state;
56	  final isOffline = current is ChatReady ? current.isOffline : false;
57	  await _chatRepository.setLastActiveSessionId(null);
58	  emit(ChatReady(sessionId: null, messages: const [], isOffline: isOffline, awaitingResponse: false));
59	}
60	```
61	
62	Bumping `_turnGeneration` here (not just in `_onMessageSubmitted`/`_onMessageRetryRequested`) ensures `_consumeTurn`'s
63	`generation != _turnGeneration` guard also catches the case where the user navigates away from a conversation
64	mid-stream (spec.md Edge Cases: "the message reflects whatever the backend ultimately recorded... rather than
65	being stuck in a stale in-progress state") — without this, an abandoned turn's later `TokenReceived`/`StreamDone`/
66	`Left` items could still pass the guard and mutate whichever conversation's `ChatReady` state is current.
67	
68	## `_loadSession` — the shared fetch-with-cache-fallback path (Clarification 3)
69	
70	```dart
71	Future<void> _loadSession(String sessionId, Emitter<ChatState> emit, {required bool isOffline}) async {
72	  final result = await _chatRepository.listMessages(sessionId);
73	  result.match(
74	    (failure) {
75	      if (failure is AuthExpiredFailure) _reauthController.add(null);
76	      final cached = _chatRepository.cachedMessages(sessionId);
77	      if (cached == null) {
78	        // Never opened while online — "the standard no-connection state instead of any content"
79	        // (Edge Cases) — only reachable here, never for the empty/no-session state above.
80	        emit(ChatReady(
81	          sessionId: sessionId, messages: const [], isOffline: isOffline,
82	          awaitingResponse: false, loadFailure: failure,
83	        ));
84	      } else {
85	        emit(ChatReady(sessionId: sessionId, messages: cached, isOffline: isOffline, awaitingResponse: false));
86	      }
87	    },
88	    (messages) async {
89	      await _chatRepository.setLastActiveSessionId(sessionId);
90	      emit(ChatReady(sessionId: sessionId, messages: messages, isOffline: isOffline, awaitingResponse: false));
91	    },
92	  );
93	}
94	```
95	
96	## `MessageSubmitted` — lazy session creation + optimistic placeholders + `emit.forEach`
97	
98	```dart
99	Future<void> _onMessageSubmitted(MessageSubmitted event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
100	  final current = state;
101	  if (current is! ChatReady || !current.canSend) return;   // composer was disabled; defensive no-op
102	
103	  if (!await _connectivityChecker.hasConnection()) {        // FR-012 — blocked client-side, never attempted
104	    return;   // composer's own isOffline flag (R8's live stream) will reflect this on its own shortly
105	  }
106	
107	  final generation = ++_turnGeneration;
108	  final now = DateTime.now();
109	  final optimisticUser = ChatMessage(
110	    id: 'local-${now.microsecondsSinceEpoch}', sessionId: current.sessionId ?? '',
111	    role: ChatRole.user, content: event.text, seq: current.messages.length,
112	    status: ChatMessageStatus.complete, retryCount: 0, createdAt: now,
113	  );
114	  final optimisticAssistant = ChatMessage(
115	    id: 'local-${now.microsecondsSinceEpoch}-response', sessionId: current.sessionId ?? '',
116	    role: ChatRole.assistant, content: '', seq: current.messages.length + 1,
117	    status: ChatMessageStatus.streaming, retryCount: 0, createdAt: now,
118	  );
119	  emit(current.copyWith(
120	    messages: [...current.messages, optimisticUser, optimisticAssistant],
121	    awaitingResponse: true,
122	  ));
123	
124	  String sessionId;
125	  if (current.sessionId == null) {
126	    final created = await _chatRepository.createSession(title: ChatTitleDeriver.derive(event.text));
127	    final maybeId = created.match((f) => null, (s) => s.id);
128	    if (maybeId == null) {
129	      if (generation != _turnGeneration) return;
130	      _failTurn(emit, created.getLeft().toNullable()!, optimisticUserId: optimisticUser.id, optimisticAssistantId: optimisticAssistant.id);
131	      return;
132	    }
133	    sessionId = maybeId;
134	    await _chatRepository.setLastActiveSessionId(sessionId);
135	  } else {
136	    sessionId = current.sessionId!;
137	  }
138	
139	  final stream = _chatRepository.sendMessage(sessionId: sessionId, content: event.text);
140	  await _consumeTurn(
141	    stream, emit, generation: generation, sessionId: sessionId,
142	    optimisticUserId: optimisticUser.id, optimisticAssistantId: optimisticAssistant.id,
143	  );
144	}
145	```
146	
147	## `MessageRetryRequested` — position-matched replacement (research.md R10)
148	
149	```dart
150	Future<void> _onMessageRetryRequested(MessageRetryRequested event, Emitter<ChatState> emit) async {
151	  final current = state;
152	  if (current is! ChatReady || current.awaitingResponse || current.sessionId == null) return;
153	  final index = current.messages.indexWhere(
154	    (m) => m.role == ChatRole.assistant && m.status == ChatMessageStatus.failed &&
155	        _userMessageIdFor(current.messages, m) == event.userMessageId,
156	  );
157	  if (index == -1) return;
158	  if (!await _connectivityChecker.hasConnection()) return;   // FR-012
159	
160	  final generation = ++_turnGeneration;
161	  final now = DateTime.now();
162	  final placeholder = ChatMessage(
163	    id: 'local-${now.microsecondsSinceEpoch}-retry', sessionId: current.sessionId!,
164	    role: ChatRole.assistant, content: '', seq: current.messages[index].seq,
165	    status: ChatMessageStatus.streaming, retryCount: current.messages[index].retryCount + 1,
166	    createdAt: now,
167	  );
168	  final updatedMessages = [...current.messages];
169	  updatedMessages[index] = placeholder;
170	  emit(current.copyWith(messages: updatedMessages, awaitingResponse: true));
171	
172	  final stream = _chatRepository.retryMessage(sessionId: current.sessionId!, userMessageId: event.userMessageId);
173	  await _consumeTurn(
174	    stream, emit, generation: generation, sessionId: current.sessionId!,
175	    optimisticUserId: null, optimisticAssistantId: placeholder.id,
176	  );
177	}
178	```
179	
180	## `_consumeTurn` — shared `emit.forEach`-driven stream consumption
181	
182	```dart
183	Future<void> _consumeTurn(
184	  Stream<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>> stream, Emitter<ChatState> emit, {
185	  required int generation, required String sessionId,
186	  required String? optimisticUserId, required String optimisticAssistantId,
187	}) async {
188	  var assistantId = optimisticAssistantId;
189	  await emit.forEach<Either<Failure, ChatStreamEvent>>(stream, onData: (result) {
190	    final latest = state;
191	    if (generation != _turnGeneration || latest is! ChatReady) return latest;   // superseded — ignore (defensive)
192	
193	    return result.match(
194	      (failure) {
195	        if (failure is AuthExpiredFailure) _reauthController.add(null);
196	        return _applyFailure(latest, assistantId, failure);
197	      },
198	      (event) => switch (event) {
199	        MessageCreated() => () {
200	            assistantId = event.assistantMessageId;
201	            return _reconcileIds(latest, optimisticUserId, event.userMessageId, optimisticAssistantId, event.assistantMessageId);
202	          }(),
203	        ContextReceived() => latest,
204	        TokenReceived(delta: final d) => _appendToken(latest, assistantId, d),
205	        StreamDone(assistantMessageId: final id, content: final c, createdAt: final t) =>
206	          _completeMessage(latest, id, c, t).copyWith(awaitingResponse: false),
207	      },
208	    );
209	  });
210	}
211	```
212	
213	- `_reconcileIds`/`_appendToken`/`_completeMessage`/`_applyFailure` are small, pure `ChatReady → ChatReady`
214	  helpers operating on `messages` by id/position — each total and independently unit-testable without any
215	  bloc/stream scaffolding.
216	- `_applyFailure` sets the matched message's `status` to `failed` (keeping whatever partial `content` had
217	  already accumulated — FR-005's "never remove, hide, or blank out a partial message") and
218	  `awaitingResponse: false`.
219	- `close()` additionally cancels `_connectivitySubscription` and closes `_reauthController` (same shape
220	  `RecordsBloc.close()` already has, plus the one new subscription).
221	
222	## Test scenarios this contract owns
223	
224	| # | Scenario | Expected |
225	|---|---|---|
226	| 1 | `ChatStarted` with no `lastActiveSessionId` stored | `ChatReady(sessionId: null, messages: [])` — no repository call beyond the one `lastActiveSessionId` read |
227	| 2 | `ChatStarted` with a stored id whose `listMessages` succeeds | `ChatReady(sessionId: ..., messages: [...])` |
228	| 3 | `ChatStarted` with a stored id whose `listMessages` fails and nothing is cached | `ChatReady(..., loadFailure: failure)` — the no-content edge case |
229	| 4 | `ChatStarted` with a stored id whose `listMessages` fails but a cache exists | `ChatReady(..., messages: <cached>)`, no `loadFailure` |
230	| 5 | `MessageSubmitted` on an empty conversation | optimistic user+assistant appended within the same synchronous `emit` (RNF01), *then* `createSession` is called with the derived title, *then* `sendMessage` |
231	| 6 | `MessageSubmitted` while offline | the composer was already disabled (`canSend == false`), so the handler is a no-op; confirms no repository call fires regardless |
232	| 7 | A full successful turn: `MessageCreated` → `TokenReceived` × N → `StreamDone` | the assistant message's `content` grows incrementally per token, then is replaced by `StreamDone.content` exactly, `status: complete`, `awaitingResponse: false` |
233	| 8 | A turn interrupted by `Left(NetworkOfflineFailure)` after 2 tokens | the assistant message keeps its 2-tokens-worth of partial content, `status: failed`, `awaitingResponse: false` (FR-005) |
234	| 9 | `MessageRetryRequested` on a `failed` message not at the end of the conversation (Edge Cases) | only that one message's position is replaced; every later message in `messages` is untouched |
235	| 10 | Two `MessageRetryRequested` dispatched back-to-back for the same message (simulating a double-tap before the composer visually disables) | the second dispatch is a no-op (`current.awaitingResponse` is already `true` from the first) |
236	| 11 | `NewConversationRequested` while a previous conversation has unsaved-to-disk messages in memory | the previous conversation's own cache entry (`ChatLocalCache`) is untouched — only `lastActiveSessionId` changes; reselecting it later still shows its full history |
237	| 12 | A `_ConnectivityChanged(false)` event arrives mid-turn (device goes offline while a response is streaming) | `isOffline` becomes `true` immediately; the in-flight turn is **not** aborted by this alone — it still resolves via whatever `sendMessage`'s own stream eventually yields (a real disconnect surfaces as its own `NetworkOfflineFailure` item from `ApiClient.sseStream`, not from this separate connectivity event) |
238	| 13 | `ConversationSelected`/`NewConversationRequested` dispatched while a turn is mid-stream for the conversation being left | the in-flight turn's later `TokenReceived`/`StreamDone`/`Left` items are ignored (generation mismatch) — the newly-loaded conversation's state is never mutated by the abandoned turn |
